      <div type="clause" n="32">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 32</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="66" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVIIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.22"/> folcleasunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.23"/> gewyrce, ⁊ hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.24"/> on hine geresp<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.25"/> weorðe, mid nanum leohtran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.26"/> ðinge gebete þon<hi rend="italic">ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.27"/></hi> him mon aceorfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.28"/> þa tungon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.29"/> óf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.30"/>, þæt hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.31"/> mon na undeorran weorðe moste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.32"/> lesan, ðonne hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.31"/> mon be þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.33"/> were geeahtige.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.34"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="66" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVIIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.2"/> folcleasunge gewyrce, ⁊ heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.5"/> on hine geræf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.11"/> weorðe, mid nanum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.6"/> leohtran ðinge gebete þonne him mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.2"/> aceorfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.12"/> ða tungan of, ðæt hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.1"/> món<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.13"/> nó<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.2"/> undeorran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.14"/> weorðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.15"/> moste alysan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.1"/>, ðonne mon be þæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.16"/> were geeahtige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="67" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf mon folcleasunge gewyrce, ⁊ heo on hine gerǽf weorðe, mid nanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> leohtran ðinge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.5-2"/> gebete þonne hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mon aceorfe ða tungan óf, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heo mon na undeorran wurde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.6-2"/> moste lésan, þonne heo mon be ðæm were geehtige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="67" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis publicum mendacium confingat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.17"/>, et in ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.18"/> denique firmetur, non emendetur hoc aliqua levi re, sed amputetur ei lingua, nec minori pretio redimi possit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_32.lnote.oe.19"/> quam secundum weram eius adpreciabitur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon folcleasunge gewyrce, ⁊ hio on hine geresp<ptr type="editorNote" n="27" target="#Af_32.attnote.fn.27"/> weorðe, mid nanum leohtran ðinge gebete þonne him mon aceorfe þa tungon óf, þæt hie mon na undeorran weorðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="28" target="#Af_32.attnote.fn.28"/> moste lesan<ptr type="editorNote" n="29" target="#Af_32.attnote.fn.29"/>, ðonne hie mon be þam were geeahtige<ptr type="editorNote" n="30" target="#Af_32.attnote.fn.30"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="33" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="324" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXVIIII} Gif mon folcleasunge gewyrce, ⁊ hio on hine geresp weorðe, mid nanum leohtran ðinge gebete þonne him mon aceorfe þa tungon óf, þæt hie mon na undeorran weorðe moste lesan, ðonne hie mon be þam were geeahtige.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="67" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand öffentliche Verleumdung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_32.lnote.de.1"/> bewirkt, und sie auf ihm Schuldbelastung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_32.lnote.de.2"/> wird, so büsse er mit keinem leichteren Dinge, als [dass] man ihm die Zunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_32.lnote.de.3"/> abschneide, [so] dass er sie nicht um billigeren Preis auslösen könne, als man sie je nach dem Wergeld [des Verleumders] schätzt.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_32.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone commits public slander, and it becomes a charge of guilt upon him, let him pay with nothing lighter than [that] his tongue be cut out, [so] that he could not redeem it at a cheaper price than it is valued according to [the slanderer’s] wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="77" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone utters a public slander, and it is proved against him, he shall make amends on no lighter terms than the excision of his tongue, [with the provision that] it shall not be ransomed at a cheaper price than [its value<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_32.attnote.n.1"/>], estimated according to the [man’s] wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="414" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone is guilty of public slander, and it is proved against him, it is to be compensated for with no lighter penalty than the cutting off of his tongue, with the proviso that it be redeemed at no cheaper rate than it is valued in proportion to the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="325" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone engages in public slander, and he is convicted of it, let him pay with no lighter settlement than that one should cut out his tongue, nor shall it be redeemed for a lesser worth than is reckoned according to his <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_4">III Eg 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_52">Af 52</ref> <quote>32 (ref. 52)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="283"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-40">Af El 40</ref> <quote>Af 32; Cod. Theod. ... though note also Af Int 40, 44.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="283"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-44">Af El 44</ref> <quote>Af 32; Cod. Theod. ... though note also Af Int 40, 44.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><label>same fashion</label> <ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6</ref> <quote>In the same fashion, Ine §18 and §38 and Alfred §7 require amputation of the hand for theft.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_52">Af 52</ref> <quote>The tongue would be redeemed at 1/3 of the value of the wergild; c.f. §56.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><label>same fashion</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_18">Ine 18</ref> <quote>In the same fashion, Ine §18 and §38 and Alfred §7 require amputation of the hand for theft.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="325"><label>same fashion</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_37">Ine 37</ref> <quote>In the same fashion, Ine §18 and §38 and Alfred §7 require amputation of the hand for theft.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="314"><label>same penalty</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_4">III Eg 4</ref> <quote>but Af 32 decreed the same for 'folcleasunge', which Whitelock renders 'public slander'</quote></note>
